      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:51:8",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ لِي أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) يَا رَبِيعُ إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ لَيَصْدُقُ حَتَّى يَكْتُبَهُ اللَّهُ صِدِّيقاً ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Abu Ali Al Ashary, from Muhammad Bin Salim, from Ahmad Bin Al Nazar Al Khazzaz, from his grandfather Al Rabie Bin Sa’ad who said, ",
          "‘Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> said to me: ‘O Rabie! Let the man be truthful until Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Writes him as a truthful one’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "8. Abu Ali al-Ash’ari has narrated from Muhammad ibn Salim from Ahmad ibn al- Nadr al-Khazzaz from his grandfather al-Rabi’ ibn Sa’d who has said the following: “Once abu Ja’far (a.s.) said to me, ‘O Rab’i, a man must keep speaking the truth until Allah writes him down as a truthful one.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
